It has been proposed many times that mirrors should provide
reflection. Of course, given the prevalence of nymphs, that would be
unbalancing. But it seems to me that if a wielded mirror gave
reflection, but shattered after a single use (or perhaps had a
significant chance of shattering after each use), game balance would
be maintained. It would give games a little more flavor, I think.

What do you think? Also, should the character take the usual luck
penalty when the mirror shatters, or should it not apply since the
character didn't directly break the mirror him/herself?

I'd code up a patch myself, but there doesn't seem to be much of a
point to patches for vanilla Nethack anymore. Maybe the maintainers of
the several popular variants could implement this idea.

